# CODEOWNERS — required reviewers per path.
#
# Every PR that touches these paths must be approved by a listed owner
# before it can merge. Configure branch protection on `main` in the
# GitHub repo settings to enforce this:
#
#   Settings → Branches → Branch protection rules → main
#     [x] Require a pull request before merging
#     [x] Require approvals (1)
#     [x] Require review from Code Owners
#     [x] Require status checks to pass before merging (select CI jobs)
#     [x] Restrict who can push to matching branches  (only maintainers)
#
# The pattern below makes the maintainer the default owner for every
# file. Add specialised owners per path as the project grows.

# Default — owns everything
*       @rambokkisa

# Critical surfaces — extra scrutiny suggested. Same owner today; split
# when other maintainers join.
/app/auth/             @rambokkisa
/app/db/migrations/    @rambokkisa
/app/connectors/       @rambokkisa
/.github/              @rambokkisa
/Dockerfile            @rambokkisa
/docker-compose.yml    @rambokkisa
/pyproject.toml        @rambokkisa
/LICENSE               @rambokkisa
/NOTICE                @rambokkisa
/SECURITY.md           @rambokkisa
